[{"id":"VRCE-2-59-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":59,"verse":1,"english":"When the night has gone away, on the morning of the next day, eulogists, accomplished ards, genealogists skilled in reciting, and singers versed musical permutation, in presenting themselves at the place of the sovereign, began to perform separately. And as they eulogized the monarch with benedictions loudly uttered, the palace resounded with the sounds of the eulogies.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.884,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-65-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2059001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2b9206038a53fc7125f0db9de310895484ef0b9a94efdfb725915287b5eb9d86","compact":"a82403de6f016afc614b69e88febb05a0af8a81a7baa6f6fd0b762cfe8351951","nasal":"114ea963ed9f675e5b6bb29571c11a530e243ceebcd16f43f85503fe81b05fd8"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-59-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":59,"verse":2,"english":"And as on former occasions, men practising purity and well up in serving, with numerous women and eunuchs entered appearance.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-65-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2059002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a8d387ec99859988649f67da396d5eb460812cfbc41a910ebdce714599e3fb96","compact":"eb6dd3cc223c1685d17a8329875886360a73b94f4811823f680715976c7106e0","nasal":"eb6dd3cc223c1685d17a8329875886360a73b94f4811823f680715976c7106e0"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-59-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":59,"verse":3,"english":"Persons acquainted with the ceremonials connected with bath, according to the ordinance and in due time, in golden vessels brought water impregnated with Hair sandal powder.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-65-5"],